# L §5.14.1 (2.1-C7b-20, open for G2): where a start pad takes with the day's first batch (E §4.2 steps 0-2), an
# arrival rule's read of bal(x, d start) of q at that place has no single point: before the pad, or after it, which
# takes with the batch the arrival is in.  As L5_14_1_arrival_reads_start, with a reading of dep at 2026-03-01 start
# that pads (450.00 against 400.00 booked; the model's on moved to 2026-10-01 so the cut sees it): REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED, the arrival refused, so konto's parts are refused from
# there.  The user chooses at G2.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w prorata
kind interests: transfers
kind tomeks: transfers
input k0: int
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place dep: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input i1_day: date
input i1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule income beats base, t = bal(dep, m.day start) of p / bal(dep, m.day start) when m in interests
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to dep amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to dep amount t1_amt
move i1: interests
  on i1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount i1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, k0

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[dep] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 300.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  i1_day = 2026-03-01
  i1_amt = 40.00 PLN
  k0 = 0

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-01-01
  pad dep from world
  stated[dep] = 450.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start
=== expect
q: (refused: REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.14.1: a start-of-day read of parts at dep, whose start pad takes with the day's first batch, refused: REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.14.1: a start-of-day read of parts at dep, whose start pad takes with the day's first batch, 0)
...
